texts.

Hellproof does not vendor, copy, or link against any of the source code
listed below. The generic Cairo crates (`cairo/crates/**`) are original,
clean-room implementations of well-known, license-agnostic algorithms (fixed
point arithmetic, BAM angles, BSP traversal, blockmaps, finite state
machines) written without reading or copying GPL-licensed source, per
PLAN.md decision A10. The Doom-specific crates (`cairo/doom/**`) reimplement
game rules and data whose *design* (state machines, formulas, data layout)
is derived from the public-domain-adjacent knowledge of the original Doom
engine and its GPL-licensed descendants; because that derivation is close
enough to constitute a derivative work in the sense of copyright law, those
crates are released under GPL-2.0-only, the license of their primary
upstream (linuxdoom-1.10), as decided in RISKS.md R9-A1.

